# Always Use Braces

In JavaScript and TypeScript, always use block bodies with braces. Do not rely on implicit returns or single-line bodies without braces.

## Arrow functions

Use a block body. Return values explicitly when needed.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — implicit return / omitted braces
const log = () => console.log("something");
const double = (n: number) => n * 2;

// ✅ GOOD
const log = () => {
  console.log("something");
};

const double = (n: number) => {
  return n * 2;
};
```

## Control flow

Always wrap `if`, `else`, `for`, `while`, `do`, and `switch` bodies in braces.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
if (condition) return;
else console.log("something");

for (const item of items) process(item);

// ✅ GOOD
if (condition) {
  return;
} else {
  console.log("something");
}

for (const item of items) {
  process(item);
}
```

## Methods and callbacks

Apply the same rule inside object methods, class methods, and callbacks.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
array.map((item) => item.id);

// ✅ GOOD
array.map((item) => {
  return item.id;
});
```

When editing existing code in these files, expand braceless or implicit-return forms to match this style.
